course: dictionary
lesson: 1016
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word bonnet is a good example. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because they are its context.
explain: «She peers under his bonnet, a Toad!» Here a bonnet is a hat. The clues are «rusty black», «perched over one eye», and the washerwoman's dress and apron in the other sentences. Toad is wearing a hat, not a car part.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another place. In the UK and Australia, a bonnet is also the metal cover over a car's engine. Clues like car, engine or open the bonnet tell you which meaning is right.
fact: A bonnet can be a hat tied under the chin with ribbons, worn by babies or by women in the past.
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, the bonnet of a car is the metal cover over the engine. In the US, people say hood.
fact: In Scotland, a bonnet is a soft flat cap worn by men.
fact: Phrases change the meaning too: an Easter bonnet is a decorated hat, and to have a bee in your bonnet means to keep thinking about one idea.
fact: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If «a hat» still makes sense, you are right.
exercise: «For his money Toad gets a cotton print gown, an apron, a shawl, and a rusty black bonnet.» What is a bonnet here? | The metal cover over an engine | A soft flat cap worn by men | *A hat tied under the chin with ribbons | A bee that keeps buzzing
exercise: Ahmed in Sydney says, «Can you check the bonnet? The car is making a funny noise.» What does bonnet mean here? | A hat for a sunny day | A cotton dress | A soft cap worn in Scotland | *The metal cover over the engine
exercise: Which sentence uses bonnet to mean an idea you keep thinking about? | Babies wear soft bonnets in winter | Mum wore a bonnet to the Easter parade | Open the bonnet and check the oil | *Grandad has a bee in his bonnet about the weather
test: «...if Toad pays her well, she will give him her dress and bonnet...» In this sentence, a bonnet is | A soft flat cap worn in Scotland | *A hat that goes with a dress | The metal cover over an engine | A lid on a saucepan
test: What is the best way to check the meaning you have picked for bonnet? | Pick the longest meaning you can find | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Look only at the first letter | Spell the word backwards
exam: Tom says bonnet always means a baby's hat. Is he right? | Yes, a bonnet is only ever a baby's hat | *No, a bonnet can also be a car's engine cover or a soft cap worn in Scotland | Yes, but only in Australia | No, bonnets are only worn in Scotland
